WEBVTT

00:02.100 --> 00:03.480
<b>OCTOBER 12, A.D. 2096</b>

00:07.940 --> 00:11.570
<b>KYOTO NEW INTERNATIONAL
CONVENTION CENTER</b>

00:08.730 --> 00:11.570
<b>This is the venue, the new Convention Center.</b>

00:11.860 --> 00:14.320
<b>It's quite far from the city center, isn't it?</b>

00:14.570 --> 00:21.410
<b>Unlike last year, there aren't that many buildings
for criminals or saboteurs to infiltrate.</b>

00:21.700 --> 00:27.170
<b>But since it's surrounded by so much nature,
that means there are plenty of places to hide.</b>

00:27.500 --> 00:30.380
<b>If there actually aren't
any hiding places nearby,</b>

00:30.380 --> 00:33.800
<b>they're likely to set up base
at a slight distance.</b>

00:34.180 --> 00:38.220
<b>What you're saying, Yoshida,
is that we should be casting a wider net...</b>

00:38.220 --> 00:42.060
<b>than just the venue's immediate surroundings?</b>

00:42.060 --> 00:45.690
<b>Yes. We don't want a repeat
of what happened last year after all.</b>

00:45.690 --> 00:49.820
<b>So, Mikihiko, who will you be sending to do recon?</b>

00:49.820 --> 00:54.320
<b>I'll be going. And I'll be asking
Leo and Erika for protection.</b>

00:54.610 --> 00:58.120
<b>Do you think that the school can spare
its Disciplinary Committee chairman?</b>

00:58.120 --> 01:02.660
<b>I'm thinking of asking Ms. Kitayama,
who's on the guard team, to fill in for me.</b>

01:02.660 --> 01:05.250
<b>Also, I'd like you to come, too, Tatsuya.</b>

01:05.250 --> 01:06.210
<b>Fine.</b>

01:06.210 --> 01:10.460
<b>Brother, if you don't mind,
I'd like to accompany you, too.</b>

01:10.790 --> 01:12.960
<b>Even though you're
the Student Council president?</b>

01:13.380 --> 01:18.220
<b>I'd like to meet the people from the hotel
that the backup team will be staying at.</b>

01:18.930 --> 01:21.970
<b>In the meantime, I want you
to take care of the budget, Honoka.</b>

01:22.350 --> 01:23.220
<b>Huh?</b>

01:23.850 --> 01:25.850
<b>Sure, you can count on me!</b>

01:25.850 --> 01:28.270
<b>As for you, Vice President Izumi...</b>

01:28.270 --> 01:31.820
<b>I'd like you to take charge
of the Council while I'm gone.</b>

01:31.820 --> 01:35.950
<b>Please, just leave it to me!
I'll give it my best shot!</b>

01:35.950 --> 01:37.490
<b>When should we go?</b>

01:37.860 --> 01:39.740
<b>How about the weekend
before the competition,</b>

01:39.740 --> 01:43.740
<b>one night and two days
from the 20th to the 21st?</b>

01:44.040 --> 01:45.750
<b>It sounds appropriate.</b>

01:45.750 --> 01:51.710
<b>The team will consist of myself, Miyuki,
Mikihiko, Leo, Erika and Minami, so six of us.</b>

01:51.710 --> 01:53.210
<b>Me, too?</b>

01:53.210 --> 01:56.590
<b>Yes. Help Miyuki out while we're there.</b>

01:57.260 --> 01:58.970
<b>Understood!</b>

02:08.190 --> 02:09.730
<b>What's the matter?</b>

02:09.730 --> 02:12.230
<b>Right, about this news...</b>

02:12.230 --> 02:19.030
<b>MURDERED BODY BY A RIVERBANK
IN KOYOTO. SUSPECT ON THE RUN.</b>

02:14.110 --> 02:16.110
<b>A murder?</b>

02:16.110 --> 02:19.990
<b>The name of the victim is...
Mr. Saburo Nakura.</b>

02:19.990 --> 02:22.240
<b>Brother, isn't this man...</b>

03:55.420 --> 03:58.050
<b>OCTOBER 13, A.D. 2096</b>

04:02.840 --> 04:06.930
<b>What's wrong, Mayumi? All this sighing...</b>

04:10.890 --> 04:13.190
<b>I want to ask for your advice about something.</b>

04:13.600 --> 04:14.810
<b>What's up?</b>

04:15.440 --> 04:18.150
<b>You know Mr. Nakura, don't you?</b>

04:18.150 --> 04:22.190
<b>He's your bodyguard, right?
Did something happen to him?</b>

04:24.070 --> 04:25.320
<b>The thing is...</b>

04:25.320 --> 04:26.700
<b>he's been murdered.</b>

04:27.070 --> 04:28.240
<b>Murdered?!</b>

04:30.540 --> 04:31.580
<b>Yes.</b>

04:31.580 --> 04:33.330
<b>But we don't know why.</b>

04:33.830 --> 04:37.920
<b>All my father would tell me
was that he'd gone to Kyoto on business.</b>

04:38.340 --> 04:41.170
<b>I'm sure it was some shady job as usual.</b>

04:42.210 --> 04:43.590
<b>Still...</b>

04:43.590 --> 04:46.220
<b>for him to end up losing his life...</b>

04:48.220 --> 04:50.010
<b>I just...</b>

04:50.010 --> 04:53.600
<b>don't think I can sit back and let this go.</b>

04:54.440 --> 04:57.730
<b>Is there a reason why you feel that way?</b>

04:58.650 --> 05:00.610
<b>I don't have any leads yet.</b>

05:00.980 --> 05:03.940
<b>But I can't stop thinking about it!</b>

05:04.610 --> 05:07.570
<b>I don't have a lot of time I can spare.</b>

05:08.320 --> 05:09.200
<b>I know!</b>

05:09.490 --> 05:11.410
<b>Why don't you talk to Jumonji?</b>

05:13.160 --> 05:18.580
<b>The Ten Master Clans has a rule prohibiting
any collaboration unless it's cleared in a clan meeting.</b>

05:18.960 --> 05:20.920
<b>Then, how about Tatsuya?</b>

05:22.050 --> 05:24.420
<b>Wh-Why Tatsuya?</b>

05:24.760 --> 05:28.550
<b>Well, isn't this year's Thesis Competition
being held in Kyoto?</b>

05:30.050 --> 05:32.430
<b>OCTOBER 15, A.D. 2096</b>

05:32.430 --> 05:36.850
<b>Tatsuya, do you remember Mr. Nakura?</b>

05:36.850 --> 05:37.690
<b>Yes.</b>

05:38.020 --> 05:40.440
<b>My condolences for your loss.</b>

05:41.070 --> 05:43.280
<b>I am humbled by your thoughtfulness.</b>

05:43.820 --> 05:45.950
<b>So, you knew about it, then.</b>

05:46.400 --> 05:47.700
<b>I saw it on the news.</b>

05:48.490 --> 05:51.870
<b>Then, do you know how he died?</b>

05:51.870 --> 05:53.620
<b>Only that it was murder...</b>

05:53.950 --> 05:54.950
<b>That's right.</b>

05:55.290 --> 05:57.830
<b>Someone killed Mr. Nakura.</b>

05:57.830 --> 06:01.210
<b>I, for one, have no idea who that person was.</b>

06:01.670 --> 06:04.090
<b>What do you mean by "I, for one"?</b>

06:04.880 --> 06:07.590
<b>My father knows who was behind it.</b>

06:07.590 --> 06:13.600
<b>After all, Mr. Nakura was in Kyoto
to carry out a secret task ordered by my father.</b>

06:13.600 --> 06:16.850
<b>So, what is it that you want to do?</b>

06:16.850 --> 06:18.940
<b>I want to find out the truth.</b>

06:18.940 --> 06:20.860
<b>To identify the culprit, you mean?</b>

06:21.810 --> 06:23.610
<b>Yes. That's right.</b>

06:23.980 --> 06:28.820
<b>My bodyguard lost his life
on the Saegusa Family's orders.</b>

06:29.200 --> 06:32.070
<b>I don't want to look away from that fact.</b>

06:32.490 --> 06:37.120
<b>As a member of the Saegusa Family,
I want to know the whole truth!</b>

06:39.210 --> 06:41.960
<b>I'm not in a place where I can accept this!</b>

06:41.960 --> 06:45.750
<b>I can't hold my head high and say, "I am
the eldest daughter of the Saegusa Family!"</b>

06:46.960 --> 06:49.130
<b>So, what do you want from me?</b>

06:49.130 --> 06:51.720
<b>It's not as if I have
a detective's know-how...</b>

06:51.720 --> 06:55.640
<b>or connections to someone
who could help with the investigation.</b>

06:55.930 --> 06:58.480
<b>Unfortunately, I don't think
I can be of use to you.</b>

06:58.810 --> 07:02.060
<b>The culprit is most likely connected
to the incident in Yokohama!</b>

07:02.690 --> 07:05.190
<b>What do you mean
by "the incident in Yokohama"?</b>

07:05.190 --> 07:08.110
<b>Someone involved
in the Yokohama Disturbance last year.</b>

07:08.110 --> 07:11.950
<b>Mr. Nakura seemed to have been looking
into the Chinatown district lately.</b>

07:13.700 --> 07:16.700
<b>Do you understand
how dangerous this could be?</b>

07:17.160 --> 07:18.370
<b>Yes.</b>

07:18.370 --> 07:21.710
<b>Even so, I can't just sit here and do nothing.</b>

07:22.170 --> 07:24.340
<b>So, Tatsuya, please!</b>

07:24.340 --> 07:26.250
<b>I want you to give me a hand!</b>

07:28.340 --> 07:29.720
<b>Very well.</b>

07:31.840 --> 07:35.180
<b>What would you like me to do specifically?</b>

07:35.680 --> 07:39.390
<b>Tatsuya, you'll be heading to Kyoto
for security work, right?</b>

07:39.390 --> 07:42.140
<b>I'd like you to give me
some of your time while you're there.</b>

07:42.140 --> 07:44.980
<b>I want to see the spot
where Mr. Nakura was killed.</b>

07:45.360 --> 07:46.690
<b>Understood.</b>

07:46.690 --> 07:49.860
<b>Then, I'll see you on Sunday, the 21st.</b>

07:51.450 --> 07:53.660
<b>Thanks, Tatsuya.</b>

07:54.370 --> 07:56.990
<b>Do you mind if I ask you something?</b>

07:57.330 --> 08:02.120
<b>Do you know what Mr. Nakura
was wearing when he was killed?</b>

08:02.120 --> 08:06.130
<b>I'm pretty sure the police
have them in storage.</b>

08:06.130 --> 08:09.130
<b>Would it be possible to take a look at them?</b>

08:10.670 --> 08:13.880
<b>I'll try contacting
the detective who notified me.</b>

08:16.930 --> 08:18.260
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

08:18.260 --> 08:21.480
<b>I didn't think you'd be that sympathetic.</b>

08:21.890 --> 08:26.020
<b>I've agreed to assist you with this,
so I'll do everything I can.</b>

08:28.770 --> 08:32.780
<b>That's the full account
of what happened in Nara.</b>

08:32.780 --> 08:37.160
<b>So, Tatsuya's taking his job
seriously for now?</b>

08:37.620 --> 08:42.540
<b>Yes. He's been proactively advancing
the search for Gongjin Zhou...</b>

08:42.960 --> 08:46.040
<b>and I'm not seeing any signs of rebellion.</b>

08:46.040 --> 08:51.710
<b>Why didn't you ask him directly
about the details of the search operation?</b>

08:51.710 --> 08:57.550
<b>I think it would've been a good test
to see if he's truly obedient or not.</b>

08:57.850 --> 08:59.310
<b>If I may be so bold,</b>

08:59.310 --> 09:06.060
<b>I didn't believe there were grounds to do so
for the purpose you have in mind.</b>

09:06.060 --> 09:10.440
<b>It's not really anything
so grand as a purpose.</b>

09:12.820 --> 09:16.200
<b>It's not because he's my nephew.</b>

09:16.610 --> 09:21.540
<b>I just didn't think it would be in the interests
of the Yotsubas to drive that boy out.</b>

09:21.830 --> 09:28.250
<b>I believe that "Because he's my blood-related
nephew" would be a sufficient reason.</b>

09:28.250 --> 09:29.670
<b>Mr. Hayama...</b>

09:29.670 --> 09:31.300
<b>Pardon me.</b>

09:40.050 --> 09:41.350
<b>Mr. Hayama...</b>

09:44.730 --> 09:46.310
<b>Lord Kuroba...</b>

09:46.310 --> 09:48.690
<b>You wanted to see me?</b>

09:49.100 --> 09:52.690
<b>What you were just discussing
with the head...</b>

09:52.690 --> 09:56.650
<b>It was about that man,
Gongjin Zhou, was it not?</b>

09:57.150 --> 09:58.110
<b>Yes.</b>

09:58.450 --> 10:07.410
<b>I am sure you know that at this time,
Lady Miyuki's guardian is being tested.</b>

10:08.790 --> 10:11.000
<b>Yes, I am aware of that.</b>

10:11.290 --> 10:14.960
<b>I was giving her a progress report.</b>

10:15.550 --> 10:20.090
<b>As Lady Miyuki is a leading candidate
to be the next head.</b>

10:20.090 --> 10:26.930
<b>The Yotsubas must know for sure that her guardian
won't one day rise up against the family.</b>

10:26.930 --> 10:32.940
<b>It's a necessary step
the family must take for the future.</b>

10:33.690 --> 10:38.860
<b>There's no way that man has
any loyalty toward the Yotsubas!</b>

10:39.320 --> 10:45.830
<b>I have no idea why you would say that
with such certainty.</b>

10:46.500 --> 10:50.210
<b>Master Tatsuya doesn't know...</b>

10:50.210 --> 10:56.010
<b>he was nearly killed by the family
soon after birth...</b>

10:56.420 --> 10:58.920
<b>so if that's your concern,</b>

10:58.920 --> 11:02.140
<b>then you're probably jumping
at shadows.</b>

11:03.720 --> 11:04.640
<b>Hayama!</b>

11:05.260 --> 11:12.650
<b>Even I am aware he has
no shred of loyalty toward the Yotsubas.</b>

11:13.230 --> 11:19.530
<b>Knowing that, Madam assigned Tatsuya
to protect Lady Miyuki.</b>

11:22.240 --> 11:23.820
<b>Lord Kuroba...</b>

11:23.820 --> 11:27.790
<b>Loyalty is actually unnecessary.</b>

11:27.790 --> 11:30.540
<b>Only actions have any meaning.</b>

11:31.120 --> 11:34.170
<b>Tools have no need to be loyal.</b>

11:34.170 --> 11:37.510
<b>Weapons need not have souls.</b>

11:37.510 --> 11:38.800
<b>Bastard!</b>

11:38.800 --> 11:41.010
<b>Are you calling magicians "weapons"?</b>

11:41.800 --> 11:46.510
<b>You may have forgotten this,
but I, too, am a magician.</b>

11:48.560 --> 11:51.060
<b>Weapons feel no fear.</b>

11:51.390 --> 11:54.150
<b>Weapons have no anxiety.</b>

11:54.150 --> 11:59.320
<b>There's only the concern
that those things may happen.</b>

11:59.320 --> 12:04.280
<b>Can you really say that a human heart
that tries to kill innocent people...</b>

12:04.280 --> 12:07.910
<b>is any better than a soulless weapon?</b>

12:16.500 --> 12:18.050
<b>THE IRREGULAR
AT MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
ANCIENT CITY INSURRECTION PART III</b>

12:19.710 --> 12:22.090
<b>OCTOBER 20, A.D. 2096
KYOTO STATION</b>

12:22.510 --> 12:25.050
<b>Mr. Tatsuya! Ms. Miyuki! Ms. Minami!</b>

12:26.390 --> 12:27.760
<b>Good morning!</b>

12:29.640 --> 12:31.230
<b>Minoru!</b>

12:35.900 --> 12:37.310
<b>Oh my gosh!</b>

12:37.310 --> 12:41.490
<b>I can't believe someone else
as drop-dead gorgeous as Miyuki existed!</b>

12:41.490 --> 12:42.700
<b>Nice to meet you.</b>

12:43.030 --> 12:45.910
<b>I'm Minoru Kudou of Second High School.</b>

12:46.490 --> 12:51.660
<b>All right, let's leave our luggage at the hotel,
then head over to the competition venue.</b>

12:55.000 --> 12:56.500
<b>KYOTO NEW INTERNATIONAL
CONVENTION CENTER</b>

12:57.380 --> 13:01.130
<b>It doesn't look like it'll be easy
to infiltrate in a large group.</b>

13:02.010 --> 13:06.890
<b>But on the other hand, it's ideal
for small groups to disperse and hide in.</b>

13:07.890 --> 13:12.140
<b>Since they can hide in residential homes
if they're in groups of two or three.</b>

13:12.770 --> 13:16.940
<b>An old caster would have
all kinds of ways to escape notice...</b>

13:16.940 --> 13:20.440
<b>like throwing up a barrier
that impedes recognition.</b>

13:21.360 --> 13:23.690
<b>Should we split up
and walk around the area?</b>

13:24.030 --> 13:27.160
<b>If there's a barrier, I think
we could at least sense some discomfort.</b>

13:27.450 --> 13:29.660
<b>No, that wouldn't be efficient.</b>

13:30.030 --> 13:32.490
<b>If they're just going to hide
in houses in small groups,</b>

13:32.490 --> 13:38.040
<b>they'll keep it to the bare minimum,
so outsiders won't notice the barrier.</b>

13:38.040 --> 13:40.290
<b>Then, what should we do?</b>

13:40.290 --> 13:42.920
<b>I'll try casting a search spell.</b>

13:43.380 --> 13:46.180
<b>Would you mind giving me a hand,
Erika and Leo?</b>

13:46.180 --> 13:48.430
<b>Sure! Leave it to me!</b>

13:48.760 --> 13:52.060
<b>I guess there's no way out of it!
Sure, I'll do it.</b>

13:52.350 --> 13:53.680
<b>I'm counting on you.</b>

13:54.520 --> 13:55.480
<b>Tatsuya...</b>

13:55.480 --> 13:57.600
<b>Ms. Miyuki and Ms. Sakurai...</b>

13:57.600 --> 14:01.980
<b>Could you patrol the downtown area
like we discussed last week?</b>

14:02.270 --> 14:03.730
<b>Uh...</b>

14:04.110 --> 14:06.990
<b>I'll show Mr. Tatsuya and the others around.</b>

14:06.990 --> 14:11.330
<b>Since it wouldn't be good for Second High, either,
if the same thing as last year were to happen.</b>

14:15.910 --> 14:20.790
<b>The Traditionalist base closest to the direction
in which Gongjin Zhou is said to have escaped...</b>

14:20.790 --> 14:22.880
<b>is in Kuramayama.</b>

14:23.170 --> 14:25.170
<b>Would you like to go there, Mr. Tatsuya?</b>

14:25.590 --> 14:28.090
<b>No, let's head back to the city.</b>

14:28.090 --> 14:29.970
<b>You mean the middle of the city?</b>

14:29.970 --> 14:35.680
<b>Brother, do you think that Gongjin Zhou
may be hiding where there are lots of people?</b>

14:35.680 --> 14:36.640
<b>Yes.</b>

14:37.020 --> 14:41.060
<b>I see. Like hiding a tree in a forest, right?</b>

14:41.060 --> 14:46.030
<b>A Traditionalist base
in a fairly populated area...</b>

14:46.740 --> 14:50.160
<b>There are maybe three places,
including Kiyomizu Shrine.</b>

14:50.160 --> 14:52.280
<b>That's less than I thought.</b>

14:52.700 --> 14:57.410
<b>The sects that are carrying out the true traditions
hold a lot of sway in Kyoto.</b>

14:57.830 --> 15:02.920
<b>So, the "in-name-only" emerging sects
have been driven into the nearby mountains.</b>

15:04.340 --> 15:05.960
<b>Master Minoru...</b>

15:05.960 --> 15:09.260
<b>Why would the Traditionalists of Kyoto
who are in such a situation...</b>

15:09.260 --> 15:16.520
<b>protect a foreign magician who's brought
numerous disasters onto Japan?</b>

15:16.520 --> 15:21.600
<b>This is just speculation, but deep down,
they probably wanted to turn him away.</b>

15:21.600 --> 15:28.030
<b>But the Traditionalists were in so deep
with Gongjin Zhou that they couldn't get out of it.</b>

15:28.360 --> 15:31.700
<b>Meaning there was a reason
why they couldn't cut ties with him?</b>

15:31.700 --> 15:36.790
<b>The Traditionalists were being fed a supply
of defected tacticians by Gongjin Zhou.</b>

15:36.790 --> 15:41.000
<b>On the surface, it looks like
the Traditionalists were helping Gongjin Zhou...</b>

15:41.000 --> 15:43.420
<b>but the reality seems to be that...</b>

15:43.420 --> 15:46.800
<b>Gongjin Zhou was helping
the Traditionalists to bolster their forces.</b>

15:50.800 --> 15:55.800
<b>HIGASHIYAMA WARD</b>

15:51.300 --> 15:53.340
<b>Let's start by going to Kiyomizu Shrine.</b>

15:53.340 --> 15:55.140
<b>Let's search the downtown area.</b>

16:06.980 --> 16:08.400
<b>It looks like they're here.</b>

16:08.400 --> 16:09.820
<b>From the mountains?</b>

16:10.650 --> 16:12.950
<b>The only presence I'm detecting
is in the mountains...</b>

16:13.450 --> 16:16.200
<b>but it's not a given that the enemy
will only emerge from there.</b>

16:16.200 --> 16:20.250
<b>And it might not just be humans
that attack us. Watch your backs.</b>

16:33.470 --> 16:34.220
<b>I'll handle it!</b>

16:45.940 --> 16:47.400
<b>What are they, ninjas?</b>

16:51.650 --> 16:52.650
<b>Interesting!</b>

16:56.530 --> 17:00.080
<b>Leo, keep your heart hot
and your mind cool, okay?</b>

17:00.080 --> 17:01.910
<b>Sorry! I owe you one!</b>

17:04.790 --> 17:08.590
<b>And sorry, Mikihiko! I'm supposed
to be protecting you, but you protected me!</b>

17:08.590 --> 17:11.380
<b>Hey, you protected me
from that surprise attack.</b>

17:11.710 --> 17:13.470
<b>We've got each other's backs.</b>

17:13.720 --> 17:16.970
<b>Okay! Let's leave it at that, then!</b>

17:22.810 --> 17:25.020
<b>Leave the enemy on the side to me!</b>

17:25.020 --> 17:26.730
<b>I'll back you up!</b>

17:27.480 --> 17:29.360
<b>Let's go, dammit!</b>

17:51.750 --> 17:52.710
<b>Oh, crap!</b>

18:08.810 --> 18:09.690
<b>A clone?</b>

18:22.450 --> 18:24.160
<b><i>Thunder Child!</i></b>

18:39.220 --> 18:40.720
<b>Is that the last of them?</b>

18:41.050 --> 18:44.310
<b>Doesn't seem like reinforcements
are on the way right now.</b>

18:44.720 --> 18:47.180
<b>Still, who would've thought
they'd send ninjas?</b>

18:47.560 --> 18:49.190
<b>You mean ninjutsu users.</b>

18:49.190 --> 18:55.940
<b>KURAMAYAMA</b>

18:49.190 --> 18:55.940
<b>SAKYO WARD
KYOTO NEW
INTERNATIONAL
CONVENTION
CENTER</b>

18:49.650 --> 18:53.440
<b>There was a base in Kuramayama
built by Ancient Magic users...</b>

18:53.440 --> 18:55.940
<b>who practiced ninjutsu.</b>

18:55.940 --> 18:59.360
<b>I think these people
must be casters from there.</b>

18:59.360 --> 19:01.620
<b>Oh yeah? Is that the story, then?</b>

19:01.620 --> 19:03.080
<b>Interesting!</b>

19:03.330 --> 19:06.450
<b>It never gets boring
being around you guys!</b>

19:07.960 --> 19:08.870
<b>Is that the enemy?</b>

19:15.460 --> 19:16.670
<b>Compound-Forms?</b>

19:16.670 --> 19:17.420
<b>No!</b>

19:18.220 --> 19:20.550
<b>These are water-based puppet spell demons!</b>

19:20.550 --> 19:21.930
<b>They've got actual bodies!</b>

19:25.970 --> 19:28.430
<b>Hey, they're no big deal!</b>

19:34.270 --> 19:35.190
<b>Whoa!</b>

19:37.320 --> 19:38.940
<b>Oh, crap! Let's get out of...</b>

19:50.460 --> 19:52.330
<b>You can't be serious!</b>

19:53.710 --> 19:54.750
<b><i>Garuda flame!</i></b>

20:07.470 --> 20:09.560
<b>They really did a number on him.</b>

20:09.560 --> 20:14.060
<b>This one's in horrible shape, too,
but he seems to be alive.</b>

20:15.310 --> 20:16.440
<b>That's weird.</b>

20:17.070 --> 20:18.190
<b>What is?</b>

20:18.190 --> 20:20.990
<b>Why isn't the water seeping into the ground?</b>

20:32.790 --> 20:34.210
<b>What's going on?</b>

20:34.210 --> 20:36.210
<b>It's the enemy's magic!</b>

20:48.810 --> 20:50.100
<b>Xiangliu?!</b>

20:51.600 --> 20:52.600
<b>Get out of the way!</b>

21:05.570 --> 21:06.370
<b>Acid?</b>

21:06.370 --> 21:08.120
<b>No, it's a corrosive spell!</b>

21:08.120 --> 21:09.370
<b>Watch out!</b>

21:09.370 --> 21:13.620
<b>Unlike acid, it's not just the parts
that get doused with that liquid that'll melt!</b>

21:17.130 --> 21:18.670
<b><i>Where's the caster?</i></b>

21:19.250 --> 21:20.500
<b><i>Over there?</i></b>

21:21.010 --> 21:21.880
<b><i>But...</i></b>

21:25.130 --> 21:26.640
<b>Erika, Leo!</b>

21:26.640 --> 21:27.850
<b>Let's retreat for now!</b>

21:27.850 --> 21:29.390
<b>I agree with you on that!</b>

21:29.760 --> 21:31.390
<b>But how do you plan on doing that?!</b>

21:32.020 --> 21:35.900
<b><i>It may be kin to an evil deity,
but Xiangliu is a water attribute.</i></b>

21:36.650 --> 21:41.900
<b><i>If it's a spell cast by accessing
the highest-ranked water deity, Dragon God...</i></b>

21:42.440 --> 21:43.610
<b><i>But...</i></b>

21:43.610 --> 21:45.280
<b><i>can I pull it off?</i></b>

22:05.720 --> 22:07.800
<b>Masaki Ichijo?</b>

22:09.390 --> 22:10.640
<b>Are you all right?</b>

23:36.430 --> 23:40.060
<b>THE IRREGULAR
AT MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
ANCIENT CITY INSURRECTION PART IV</b>
